{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176243-working-at-cross-purposes-lovecraft-crossover","id":1176243,"title":"Working at cross-purposes [Lovecraft crossover?]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-15T04:31:26-08:00","id":1176243,"title":"Working at cross-purposes [Lovecraft crossover?]","content":"To avoid derailing the Spaceships and extraterrestial thread, i started a new topic about this quote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurelius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1175946-spaceflight-starships-extraterrestrials?p=1176010#post1176010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another option draws inspiration from on Lovecraft's short story <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Other_Gods\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;The Other Gods&quot;</a>. When the Exarchs ascended, they threw out the previous gods of Earth and took their thrones. However, the gods of Earth were not the biggest fish in the celestial pond. They <i>were</i> sufficiently powerful to deter the eldritch powers that be from simply making a meal of us though, and now that responsibility falls to their replacements. Perhaps the Abyss was created in an act of desperation to fend these Other Gods off. Even they aren't so keen on the unmaking of all truth. Of course, the Abyss is also a major threat in its own right and the Exarchs would really appreciate it if you would all just stop distracting them from dealing with all of this already. In this interpretation, it is actually possible to physically leave the domain of the Exarchs and is also a really bad idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the way it paints the exarchs something other than supreme celestial tyrants, into a more ... dare i say heroic role.<br /> <br /> Yes, they stormed heaven and cast out the gods in an act of supreme hubris; replacing the gods. They took their places, so the situation goes from &quot;small fish in a big pond&quot; to &quot;slightly bigger fish in a just as big pond&quot;, so the situation didn't really change that much. <br /> <br /> The Abyss, in my mind would be a major incursion that slipped in during the &quot;change of the guard&quot;. <br /> The alternative with the abyss being a defensive measure is interesting, but i can't wrap my head around it. I'd want to do something interesting with the &quot;Secret order of the gate&quot; in this scenario, but i'm not sure what exactly.<br /> <br /> It definitely flips quite a lot of the assumptions of the setting on their heads. <br /> <br /> How does this do to the orders? how do the roles change. The Seers and the Ladder would change enough to be unrecognizable... the Arrow, the Guardians and the Mysterium would not change that much in terms of role; <br /> <br /> You could also keep the seers and the ladder's themes pretty much intact; the seers and the ladder just working at cross purposes: the seers want to strengthen the exarchs (at any cost), which in turn protects the world from the Outer gods, while the ladder wants more mages; even if awakening (and eventually ascension) makes the Exarch's work harder in the short term (by rocking the boat).<br /> <br /> Does this alternate universe version of the Mage cosmology interest anyone else? Any other takes/ideas about how things could go in this situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T04:43:41-08:00","id":1176249,"title":"","content":"Imo, it doesn't really change anything. The Exarchs still maintain their position via symbols of tyranny, and they broke the world in their ascension or however they got into power. They're arguably doing a worse job than the gods they removed. Saying they're heroes is distracting from the fact that they weren't needed, and only took up the responsibility of &quot;defending&quot; humanity because the roles they assumed obligated them too. It's propaganda.<br /> <br /> Edit: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MovingMind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176243-working-at-cross-purposes-lovecraft-crossover#post1176243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also keep the seers and the ladder's themes pretty much intact; the seers and the ladder just working at cross purposes: the seers want to strengthen the exarchs (at any cost), which in turn protects the world from the Outer gods, while the ladder wants more mages; even if awakening (and eventually ascension) makes the Exarch's work harder in the short term (by rocking the boat).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Seers and the Ladder already work at cross purposes in pretty much the manner described without changing anything minus the bit about the Exarchs protecting the world from the Outer Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-15-2018, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T05:52:10-08:00","id":1176256,"title":"","content":"I could see the Bound and the Old Gods being renamed and re-fluffed to, say, the Starborn and the Great Old Ones. The ancient magic-eating monsters that haunt the Awakened (and are often contained by the Seers) are now extraterrestrial instead of mythological.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T06:17:42-08:00","id":1176260,"title":"","content":"There's some other room to play with this in the sources, depending on how you look at it. Like with the Dreamlands, where the Old Gods exist but the ones you have to be really afraid of are the Outer Gods.<br /> <br /> If one were to, say, commit an act of hubris and climb to the Kadath, he would be above the deities of more human-like nature but right at the doorstep of Azathoth's court and with a pissed Nyarlathotep now interested in you, Quite a clear parallel.<br /> <br /> There are more difficult crossovers to pull off, so have fun with it by all means","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-15-2018, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T06:36:22-08:00","id":1176264,"title":"","content":"Perhaps &quot;heroic&quot; is not the right word. What word would you use when someone does horrible things &lt;break reality and cast down the gods&gt;, notice the can of worms you opened &lt;the abyss/outer gods&gt; and say &quot;oops... i got to fix this&quot;? <br /> <br /> &quot;I just wanted to be king of the universe; i thought it would be easier&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> You're right in that the change can be merely cosmetic, i was theorizing about something a bit more involved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176243-working-at-cross-purposes-lovecraft-crossover?p=1176249#post1176249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exarchs still maintain their position via symbols of tyranny</div> </div> </div> </div>If you put it that way my &quot;how does this change the setting&quot; question does become trivial to answer... &quot;use something other than tyranny&quot;. I was probably going to far afield when i didn't have to","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}